Appendix D — Formal Verification Layer: Full Details

D.1 Soundness Proof (Theorem 3.1)

The SMT solver is invoked on the query \phi_h \land \mathcal{A}. If the result is unsat, then the formula is unsatisfiable. This means there is no interpretation (no assignment of real values to variables) that satisfies both \phi_h and \mathcal{A}. By soundness of the solver (assuming the theory of QF_NRA is correctly implemented), this verdict is correct. Since the true physical world must satisfy \mathcal{A} (by the soundness of our axioms), it cannot satisfy \phi_h. Hence \phi_h does not correspond to a physically realisable mechanism. ∎

D.2 Complexity of QF_NRA

The decision problem for quantifier-free non-linear real arithmetic is solvable by cylindrical algebraic decomposition (CAD) in time doubly exponential in the number of variables in the worst case. In practice, modern SMT solvers use a combination of CAD, interval constraint propagation, and linearisation. The fragment we use restricts to polynomial constraints (and approximations of transcendental functions), making it decidable.

